  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Scheduler behaviour worth knowing before reading these numbers",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "In `CompactionService.runCompaction`, a **major run replaces that tick's minor run** \u2014 it does not run alongside it. A single compactor therefore never produces concurrent minor and major activity, and any claim of \"concurrent compaction\" from a single-instance run is wrong. See `TEST_SCENARIOS.md`.\n\nThe compactor uses a `LoggingMeterRegistry`, so merge *durations* are log lines, not metrics. They are parsed out into `raw/compaction.jsonl` at collection time and appear in the generated report, not here."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Activity",
      "gridPos": {
